{"name":"Finlandia","hex":"#61755b","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[],"entries":[{"title":"Finlandia","blocks":[{"text":"Finlandia, Op. 26, is a tone poem by the Finnish composer Jean Sibelius. It was written in 1899 and revised in 1900. The piece was composed for the Press Celebrations of 1899, a covert protest against increasing censorship from the Russian Empire, and was the last of seven pieces performed as an accompaniment to a tableau depicting episodes from Finnish history. The premiere was on 2 July 1900 in Helsinki with the Helsinki Philharmonic Society conducted by Robert Kajanus. A typical performance takes between 7+1⁄2 and 9 minutes."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7a/JeanSibelius_circa1898-1900.jpg/330px-JeanSibelius_circa1898-1900.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Finlandia","wikidata":"Q644152"},{"title":"Finlandia (2000)","blocks":[{"text":"MS Finlandia is a cruiseferry owned by Rederiaktiebolaget Eckerö and operated by the Finnish ferry operator Eckerö Line. The ship operates between Tallinn and Helsinki."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e8/Finlandia_Starboard_Side_Tallinn_24_April_2014.JPG/330px-Finlandia_Starboard_Side_Tallinn_24_April_2014.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Finlandia_(2000)","wikidata":"Q3022529"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bc/Finlandia_premi%C3%A8re_%C3%A9dition.gif/250px-Finlandia_premi%C3%A8re_%C3%A9dition.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/b/bc/Finlandia_premi%C3%A8re_%C3%A9dition.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bc/Finlandia_premi%C3%A8re_%C3%A9dition.gif/250px-Finlandia_premi%C3%A8re_%C3%A9dition.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Finlandia, piano arrangement by the composer (1900). 1952 autographed copy for the Mayor of New York, Vincent Impellitteri.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AFinlandia_premi%C3%A8re_%C3%A9dition.gif"}],"sounds":{},"pictures":[{"title":"Merak tarung","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/21/Merak_tarung.jpg/500px-Merak_tarung.jpg","ratio":1.4997000599880024,"link":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Merak_tarung.jpg","share":0.225625},{"title":"Bali, Rice fields, Rice terraces in East Bali, Indonesia","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/88/Bali%2C_Rice_fields%2C_Rice_terraces_in_East_Bali%2C_Indonesia.jpg/500px-Bali%2C_Rice_fields%2C_Rice_terraces_in_East_Bali%2C_Indonesia.jpg","ratio":1.5,"link":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bali,_Rice_fields,_Rice_terraces_in_East_Bali,_Indonesia.jpg","share":0.161875},{"title":"Töölönlahti1","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5e/T%C3%B6%C3%B6l%C3%B6nlahti1.jpg/500px-T%C3%B6%C3%B6l%C3%B6nlahti1.jpg","ratio":1.3332,"link":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:T%C3%B6%C3%B6l%C3%B6nlahti1.jpg","share":0.155625},{"title":"Stamp of Finland - 1965 - Colnect 46460 - Music sheet for - Finlandia","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fe/Stamp_of_Finland_-_1965_-_Colnect_46460_-_Music_sheet_for_-_Finlandia.jpeg/500px-Stamp_of_Finland_-_1965_-_Colnect_46460_-_Music_sheet_for_-_Finlandia.jpeg","ratio":1.4237726098191215,"link":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Stamp_of_Finland_-_1965_-_Colnect_46460_-_Music_sheet_for_-_Finlandia.jpeg","share":0.095},{"title":"Zuger See SK 0009","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cb/Zuger_See_SK_0009.jpg/500px-Zuger_See_SK_0009.jpg","ratio":1.5002544529262087,"link":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Zug